        <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
             FEED CLEARED 2026-06-04. Every prior entry (0.0.7 / 0.0.6 / 0.0.2 /
             0.0.1) advertised a release whose .dmg ASSET 404'd — the GitHub
             release tags exist but the DMG assets were never published (or were
             removed). So Sparkle saw a "newer" version, tried to download it,
             and every launch failed with "Update Error". VibeDispatcher is
             pre-launch; NO downloadable release actually exists yet.

             An item-less channel = Sparkle reports "you're up to date" and never
             attempts a download → no more Update Error.

             To ship a real release: publish the signed+notarized DMG as a
             release asset FIRST, confirm its download URL returns 200, THEN add
             its <item> here. CI guard `.github/workflows/appcast-integrity.yml`
             FAILS if any advertised enclosure URL does not resolve, so a phantom
             release can never silently break the updater again.
             ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    </channel>
</rss>
